@page "/lecturer/tasks"
@layout AppLayout
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = Roles.Admin + "," + Roles.Staff)]
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Components
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Pages.Mentor
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Services
@using AuthWithAdmin.Shared.AuthSharedModels
@inject IProjectRequestsService          Requests
@inject IPendingMentorApprovalsService   Approvals
@inject IDashboardOverviewService        Overview
@inject IPersonalTasksService            PersonalTasks
@implements IDisposable

@*
    ── המשימות שלי — the lecturer's work centre ─────────────────────────────
    Visual source:  MentorTasksPage (המשימות שלי) and the finalized Lecturer
                    dashboard. Every surface is a shared M* primitive under
                    `.motiva-final`; this page declares almost nothing.

    ── AN ACTION VIEW OVER EXISTING DATA, NOT A TASK DATABASE ───────────────
    Four feeds, each read from the endpoint that already owns it, each row
    still belonging to its own entity and still opening that entity's own
    screen. Nothing is copied into a new table, nothing is merged into
    PersonalTasks, and no new task type exists.

      בקשות הדורשות החלטה      GET api/project-requests
                               → /management/requests
      הגשות הדורשות טיפול       GET api/task-submissions/pending-mentor-approvals
                               → /lecturer/submissions
      משימות אישיות            GET api/projects/personal-tasks
                               → the shared editor, in place

    Every one of those endpoints existed and was already authorised for this
    role — verified live, not assumed. Nothing was added to the server, the
    DTOs or the schema.

    ── WHICH REQUESTS COUNT AS "MINE", AND WHOSE RULE THAT IS ───────────────
    RequestsManagement.BucketOf() is the product's own classifier, and this
    page uses the same three buckets rather than inventing a fourth:

      decision  New · InProgress · WaitingForStaff · NeedsInfo ·
                PendingLecturerDecision      → the lecturer's
      mentor    PendingMentorRecommendation  → blocked on a MENTOR, not shown
      done      Resolved · Closed            → not shown

    So a request that is waiting on someone else never appears here. Reusing
    the existing helper's rule — rather than writing a narrower one — is what
    keeps this page and /management/requests from disagreeing about what is
    open.

    ONE PRE-EXISTING DISCREPANCY, REPORTED NOT FIXED. The nav badge and the
    dashboard chip read Summary.OpenRequests, which the server computes as
    "status NOT IN (Resolved, Closed)" — that includes the three requests
    waiting on a mentor. So the badge can read 18 while this page's tab reads
    15. Both are correct about their own question; reconciling them would mean
    changing a server-side count, which this pass must not do.

    ── WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE ────────────────────────────────────────
      * The census, the health split, the four counter chips and every other
        aggregate. They answer "how is the portfolio", which is the
        dashboard's question. This page answers "what do I do next", and a
        number with no row under it is not something you can do.
      * PendingMentorRecommendation requests and MentorAttention's feeds —
        both are other people's queues.
      * Overdue STUDENT tasks. Summary.OverdueTasks and
        Charts.OverdueByMilestone are real and already on the dashboard, but
        they are students' tasks in aggregate: there is no per-task row a
        lecturer can act on, and no route that would open one. A section that
        cannot link anywhere is a metric wearing a row's clothes.
      * PROJECTS THE SERVER SCORED AtRisk. This page carried them as a fourth
        section and no longer does: a team's risk is a state of a team, and
        הצוותים שלי is the screen that owns teams. Two homes for one fact is
        the duplication this page exists to remove, not to create. The feed
        and its endpoint call are gone from here; that screen is untouched.

    ── DUAL-ROLE, AND WHAT מצב מנחה DOES ────────────────────────────────────
    THE WORKSPACE IS PERMANENT. This page, its route, its three panes and every
    one of its feeds exist in BOTH modes. Nothing here is gated on מצב מנחה
    ("guidance mode") being on or off — a lecturer's queue does not stop being
    their queue when they put a mentor hat on, so the page is never hidden,
    emptied or disabled by a mode.

    GUIDANCE MODE IS A SCOPE, AND ONLY A SCOPE. When a user who genuinely holds
    BOTH roles is in מצב מנחה, the two project-keyed feeds that can meaningfully
    be narrowed are narrowed to the projects that user actually mentors:

        בקשות הדורשות החלטה       filtered by ProjectId ∈ guidance set
        הגשות הדורשות טיפול        filtered by ProjectId ∈ guidance set
        משימות אישיות             NEVER filtered; they are the person's own,
                                  keyed on UserId alone and true in both modes

    ONE RULE, BOTH WORK FEEDS. Every feed that describes work arriving from
    a project is scoped the same way, through the same InGuidanceScope predicate
    on the same guidance set — so the three panes can never disagree about what
    "in my guidance context" means. Personal tasks are the deliberate exception
    and the only one: they are not work arriving from a project, they are the
    person's own list.

    The guidance set is GET api/dashboard?scope=mentor — the mentor dashboard's
    own endpoint, whose scope the SERVER resolves from the caller's roles. No
    new API, no new rule, and no way for this page to widen what the user may
    see. It is fetched only when guidance is actually active; the rest of the
    time the scope is null and every feed passes through whole.

    BOTH HALVES OF GuidanceActive MATTER. UserModeService.CurrentMode is a
    process-wide static, so a Staff-only lecturer can hold a stale "mentor"
    value; IsDualRole is what makes the scope inert for anyone with no guidance
    context. It also avoids a real trap — api/dashboard?scope=mentor answers a
    Staff-ONLY caller with the LECTURER scope, so filtering on it for such a
    user would narrow nothing while looking like it had.

    MentorTasksPage remains the mentor's own three ProjectMentors-scoped feeds
    at /mentor/tasks; the two pages do not merge, and the mentor rail still
    points there in מצב מנחה.
*@

@* ── המשימות שלי — THE MENTOR'S WORKSPACE, WITH THE LECTURER'S FEEDS ──────
     This page went to a Kanban board and then to a Bento grid, and both
     were wrong for the same reason: they were compositions invented for
     this screen alone, so /mentor/tasks and /lecturer/tasks stopped being
     the same product's answer to the same question. It is MentorTasksPage's
     composition again — header bleed with the switcher on the title row,
     one viewport-filling workspace row, the incoming queues stacked in the
     wide column and משימות אישיות as a full-height rail, every panel
     scrolling inside itself so the page never does.

     ── THREE FEEDS, NOT FOUR ────────────────────────────────────────────
     צוותים בסיכון IS GONE. A team at risk is a state of a team, and
     הצוותים שלי is the screen that owns teams — carrying it here as well
     made one fact live in two places, which is the duplication this page
     was created to remove. The feed, its cards, its health gauge and its
     icon signals are all deleted; nothing about הצוותים שלי is touched.

       בקשות הדורשות החלטה   GET api/project-requests
                             → /management/requests
       הגשות הדורשות טיפול   GET api/task-submissions/pending-mentor-approvals
                             → /lecturer/submissions
       משימות אישיות         GET api/projects/personal-tasks
                             → the shared editor, in place

     The lecturer's three map onto the mentor's three: something teams have
     sent that is waiting on a decision, something waiting on a review, and
     the person's own list. Order follows obligation — a decision only this
     person can make comes before a review someone else is holding.

     ── THE FILTER IS THE MENTOR'S, NOT THE KANBAN'S ─────────────────────
     The tabs were הכל / דורש טיפול / באיחור / קרוב למועד, a cross-workspace
     priority lens built for a board of four columns. It is replaced by the
     mentor's own switcher — הכל plus one tab per section, each carrying its
     count — because that is what this workspace's control is, and because a
     lens that needed four columns to justify itself does not survive the
     board it was built for.

     Priority is still scannable, and by better means than a filter: each
     tab shows its queue's size, and every row carries its waiting age on
     the shared three-step ladder (see AgeChip).

     ── WHAT IS PRESERVED FROM THE REFINEMENTS ───────────────────────────
       * rows carry ONE short context line and nothing else
       * the waiting-age chip escalates neutral → brand tint → rose, from
         MentorAttention's single shared threshold
       * count bubbles are the product-wide `.motiva-count` — gradient tint,
         dark digits, never violet ink
       * headings are dark ink, and there is no coloured bar on a row
       * a click INSPECTS in place; the panel's CTA is what navigates

     ── UNCHANGED ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     No endpoint, DTO, permission, route, filter rule or scoping rule. The
     guidance scope and RequestsManagement's bucket rule are byte-for-byte
     what they were. *@

@* ── The section glyphs' ink ──
     ONE <linearGradient>, referenced by all three icons. An SVG stroke cannot
     take a CSS gradient — `stroke` resolves a paint server, not a background —
     so the gradient has to exist as a document node and be referenced by id.
     Defining it once here rather than inside each glyph keeps the three marks
     provably identical and avoids three competing ids in one document.

     Rendered outside the loading branch so the reference is never dangling:
     an icon that paints before its paint server exists renders with no stroke
     at all. `to left` in SVG terms is x1=1 → x2=0, violet at the reading start
     to cyan at the reading end, matching --motiva-gradient-signature. *@
<svg class="lt-grad-def" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <defs>
        <linearGradient id="ltIconGradient" x1="1" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
            <stop offset="0%"   stop-color="#6D28F5" />
            <stop offset="60%"  stop-color="#2E63E8" />
            <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#0FA8C2" />
        </linearGradient>
    </defs>
</svg>

<div class="lt-header-bleed">
    @* The reference puts the switcher on the title row, pushed to the
       reading end — not on a full-width row of its own. *@
    <MPageHeader Variant="MPageHeader.HeaderVariant.Compact"
                 Title="המשימות שלי"
                 Subtitle="בקשות, הגשות ותזכורות אישיות שממתינות לפעולה שלך.">
        <Actions>
            @if (!_loading)
            {
                <MFilterTabs Tabs="@FilterTabs"
                             ActiveKey="@ActiveTabKey"
                             OnSelect="SelectFocus"
                             AriaLabel="סינון תור העבודה" />
            }
        </Actions>
    </MPageHeader>
</div>

<div class="lt-body">

    @if (_loading)
    {
        <MLoadingState Label="טוענת את המשימות…" />
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="lt-workspace @WorkspaceClass">

            @if (ShowsPrimary)
            {
                <div class="lt-primary">

                @* ── 1. בקשות הדורשות החלטה ── *@
                @if (Shows(Section.Requests))
                {
                    <section id="requests" class="lt-pane @QuietWhenEmpty(_requests.Count)">
                        <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Fill="true">
                            <div class="lt-card">
                                <div class="lt-card-head">
                                    <MSectionHeading Class="lt-head" Text="בקשות הדורשות החלטה"
                                                     Count="@CountLabel(_requests.Count)"
                                                     LinkHref="/management/requests" LinkText="לכל הבקשות">
                                        <Icon>
                                            <span class="lt-ico">
                                                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="url(#ltIconGradient)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                                    <path d="M4 13h4l1.4 2.6h5.2L16 13h4"></path>
                                                    <path d="M4.6 12.6 6.9 5.4A1.6 1.6 0 0 1 8.4 4.3h7.2a1.6 1.6 0 0 1 1.5 1.1l2.3 7.2v4.8a1.8 1.8 0 0 1-1.8 1.8H6.4a1.8 1.8 0 0 1-1.8-1.8z"></path>
                                                </svg>
                                            </span>
                                        </Icon>
                                    </MSectionHeading>
                                </div>

                                <MScrollArea Tabbable="false">

                                    @if (_requests.Count == 0)
                                    {
                                        <MEmptyState Title="אין בקשות שדורשות את החלטתך."
                                                     Description="בקשות שממתינות להחלטתך יופיעו כאן."
                                                     Class="lt-empty" />
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <MRowList AriaLabel="בקשות הדורשות החלטה">
                                            @foreach (var r in _requests.Take(PreviewCount))
                                            {
                                                @* Opens the shared Quick View OVER this queue. The
                                                   panel's CTA is what navigates, to the same
                                                   /management/requests this row used to open. *@
                                                var req = r;
                                                <MRow OnClick="@(() => Inspect(req))"
                                                      Primary="@r.Title"
                                                      Secondary="@OneOf(r.TeamName, r.ProjectTitle)"
                                                      Status="@AgeChip(WaitingLabel(DaysOpen(r)), MentorAttentionRows.AgeVariant(DaysOpen(r)))"
                                                      Tooltip="@Details(r.Title, RequestStatuses.Label(r.Status), TypeLabel(r.RequestType), r.TeamName, r.ProjectTitle, MentorTime.AgoLabel(r.CreatedAt))"
                                                      AriaLabel="@($"{r.Title} — {RequestStatuses.Label(r.Status)}, {WaitingLabel(DaysOpen(r))}. הצגת פרטי הבקשה")" />
                                            }
                                        </MRowList>
                                    }
                                </MScrollArea>

                                @if (_requests.Count > PreviewCount)
                                {
                                    <div class="lt-expand">
                                        <a class="lt-more" href="/management/requests">
                                            לכל הבקשות<span class="lt-more-n">@_requests.Count</span>
                                        </a>
                                    </div>
                                }
                            </div>
                        </MCard>
                    </section>
                }

                @* ── 2. הגשות הדורשות טיפול ── *@
                @if (Shows(Section.Approvals))
                {
                    <section id="approvals" class="lt-pane @QuietWhenEmpty(_approvals.Count)">
                        <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Fill="true">
                            <div class="lt-card">
                                <div class="lt-card-head">
                                    <MSectionHeading Class="lt-head" Text="הגשות הדורשות טיפול"
                                                     Count="@CountLabel(_approvals.Count)"
                                                     LinkHref="/lecturer/submissions" LinkText="לכל ההגשות">
                                        <Icon>
                                            <span class="lt-ico">
                                                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="url(#ltIconGradient)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                                    <path d="M14 3.2H7.4a1.9 1.9 0 0 0-1.9 1.9v13.8a1.9 1.9 0 0 0 1.9 1.9h9.2a1.9 1.9 0 0 0 1.9-1.9V7.6z"></path>
                                                    <path d="M14 3.2v4.4h4.5"></path>
                                                    <path d="m9.1 14.4 1.9 1.9 3.9-3.9"></path>
                                                </svg>
                                            </span>
                                        </Icon>
                                    </MSectionHeading>
                                </div>

                                <MScrollArea Tabbable="false">

                                    @if (_approvals.Count == 0)
                                    {
                                        <MEmptyState Title="אין הגשות שתקועות אצל מנחה."
                                                     Description="הגשות שממתינות לאישור מנחה יופיעו כאן."
                                                     Class="lt-empty" />
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <MRowList AriaLabel="הגשות הדורשות טיפול">
                                            @foreach (var a in _approvals.Take(PreviewCount))
                                            {
                                                @* DaysWaiting is the SERVER's figure, and the same one
                                                   the submissions screen gates "תזכורת למנחה" on at
                                                   >= 3 — which is also MentorAttention's single
                                                   threshold, so the chip escalates at the moment the
                                                   action unlocks. Never באיחור: a mentor approval has
                                                   no deadline to be late for. *@
                                                var app = a;
                                                <MRow OnClick="@(() => Inspect(app))"
                                                      Primary="@a.TaskTitle"
                                                      Secondary="@OneOf(a.TeamName, a.ProjectTitle)"
                                                      Status="@AgeChip(WaitingLabel(a.DaysWaiting), MentorAttentionRows.AgeVariant(a.DaysWaiting))"
                                                      Tooltip="@Details(a.TaskTitle, WaitingLabel(a.DaysWaiting), a.TeamName, a.ProjectTitle, a.MilestoneTitle, MentorLabel(a.MentorName))"
                                                      AriaLabel="@($"{a.TaskTitle} — {WaitingLabel(a.DaysWaiting)}. הצגת פרטי ההגשה")" />
                                            }
                                        </MRowList>
                                    }
                                </MScrollArea>

                                @if (_approvals.Count > PreviewCount)
                                {
                                    <div class="lt-expand">
                                        <a class="lt-more" href="/lecturer/submissions">
                                            לכל ההגשות<span class="lt-more-n">@_approvals.Count</span>
                                        </a>
                                    </div>
                                }
                            </div>
                        </MCard>
                    </section>
                }

                </div>
            }

            @if (Shows(Section.Personal))
            {
                <div class="lt-rail">
                @* ── 3. משימות אישיות ── *@
                <section id="personal" class="lt-pane">
                    <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Fill="true">
                        <div class="lt-card">
                            <div class="lt-card-head">
                                <MSectionHeading Class="lt-head" Text="משימות אישיות"
                                                 Count="@CountLabel(_personalOpen.Count)">
                                    <Icon>
                                        <span class="lt-ico">
                                            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="url(#ltIconGradient)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                                <rect x="4" y="4" width="16" height="16" rx="4.5"></rect>
                                                <path d="m8.6 12.1 2.3 2.3 4.5-4.5"></path>
                                            </svg>
                                        </span>
                                    </Icon>
                                    <Trailing>
                                        @* PERSONAL tasks only, and it sits on their own heading.
                                           These carry a real DueDate, so באיחור is a true
                                           statement about them; it would not be about a request
                                           or a submission, neither of which has a deadline. *@
                                        @if (OverdueCount > 0)
                                        {
                                            <span class="lt-overdue">@OverdueCount באיחור</span>
                                        }
                                        <button type="button" class="lt-add"
                                                title="הוספת משימה" aria-label="הוספת משימה אישית"
                                                @onclick="OpenNewTask">
                                            <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                                 stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"
                                                 aria-hidden="true">
                                                <path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path>
                                            </svg>
                                        </button>
                                    </Trailing>
                                </MSectionHeading>
                            </div>

                            <MScrollArea Tabbable="false">

                                @if (_visiblePersonal.Count == 0)
                                {
                                    <MEmptyState Title="אין תזכורות פתוחות."
                                                 Description="תזכורות שתוסיף/י לעצמך יופיעו כאן."
                                                 Class="lt-empty" />
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <MRowList AriaLabel="משימות אישיות">
                                        @foreach (var t in _visiblePersonal)
                                        {
                                            var id = t.Id;
                                            <MRow Class="@(t.IsDone ? "lt-task-done" : null)"
                                                  Secondary="@OneOf(t.TeamName, t.ProjectTitle)"
                                                  Status="@DueChip(t)"
                                                  Tooltip="@Details(t.Title, MentorTime.DeadlineLabel(t.DueDate), t.TeamName, t.ProjectTitle, t.Description)">
                                                <Leading>
                                                    <button type="button"
                                                            class="lt-check @(t.IsDone ? "lt-check-on" : "")"
                                                            role="checkbox"
                                                            aria-checked="@t.IsDone"
                                                            aria-label="@($"סימון \"{t.Title}\" כהושלמה")"
                                                            disabled="@(_togglingId == id)"
                                                            @onclick="@(() => ToggleAsync(id))">
                                                        @if (t.IsDone)
                                                        {
                                                            <svg width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                                                                 stroke-width="3.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                                                                <path d="m5 13 4.5 4.5L19 7"></path>
                                                            </svg>
                                                        }
                                                    </button>
                                                </Leading>
                                                <PrimaryContent>
                                                    @* The title opens the editor. A personal task is the
                                                       lecturer's OWN item, so unlike a request or a
                                                       submission it is editable in place — the checkbox
                                                       stays a separate hit target so completing a task
                                                       never risks opening a dialog. *@
                                                    <button type="button" class="lt-task-title lt-task-edit"
                                                            @onclick="@(() => OpenEditTask(t))"
                                                            aria-label="@($"עריכת \"{t.Title}\"")">
                                                        @t.Title
                                                    </button>
                                                </PrimaryContent>
                                            </MRow>
                                        }
                                    </MRowList>
                                }

                            </MScrollArea>

                            @* Show the toggle whenever the collapsed view is actually hiding
                               something — open rows past the cap, or completed ones behind it. *@
                            @if (_personalOpen.Count > PersonalCollapsedCount || _personalDone.Count > 0)
                            {
                                <div class="lt-expand">
                                    @* An EXPANDER, not a link, and that is not an
                                       inconsistency to fix: personal reminders have no
                                       module of their own for a lecturer — יומן goes to
                                       /milestones-overview, and /mentor/calendar is the
                                       mentor's screen. There is nowhere for "לכל
                                       המשימות" to lead, so the full list opens here. *@
                                    <button type="button" class="lt-expand-btn" @onclick="TogglePersonalExpanded">
                                        @(_personalExpanded ? "הצג פחות" : "הצג הכל")
                                        @if (!_personalExpanded && HiddenPersonal > 0)
                                        {
                                            <span class="lt-more-n">@(_personalOpen.Count + _personalDone.Count)</span>
                                        }
                                    </button>
                                </div>
                            }
                        </div>
                    </MCard>
                </section>
                </div>
            }

        </div>
    }
</div>

@* ── Inspect an incoming item ──
     ONE surface for both incoming kinds, the same rule the mentor screens
     follow: a click from a queue inspects in place, and the panel's CTA is
     what navigates. Personal tasks keep their own editor below — they are
     the one feed the lecturer OWNS and edits, which is a different act. *@
<LecturerItemQuickView Item="@_inspecting"
                       OnClose="CloseInspect"
                       OnChanged="StateHasChanged" />

@* ── New / edit personal task ──
     The shared editor, not a copy: /mentor/tasks and /mentor/calendar open the
     very same component. `Projects` is left at its default empty list, because
     the server grants a task's ProjectId only through ProjectMentors — see the
     note at MentorPersonalTaskModal's project row. *@
<MentorPersonalTaskModal IsOpen="@_modalOpen"
                         EditingTask="@_editing"
                         OnClose="CloseModal"
                         OnSaved="OnTaskSaved"
                         OnDeleted="OnTaskDeleted" />

@code {
    /// <summary>The three feeds. Also the tab vocabulary — one enum, so a tab
    /// and a section cannot disagree about what they mean.</summary>
    private enum Section { Requests, Approvals, Personal }

    /// <summary>
    /// How many rows a section shows before it hands off to the full module.
    ///
    /// <para>This page is an overview, not a list: the panels no longer scroll
    /// inside themselves, so what is on screen is what the section shows and
    /// the footer action is how the rest is reached. Six is the mentor rail's
    /// own collapsed depth, used for all three so the sections cannot disagree
    /// about what "a preview" means.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>WHAT SURVIVES THE CAP IS DECIDED BY THE EXISTING ORDER, not by a
    /// new rule: requests are longest-waiting first and submissions are
    /// longest-stuck first, both set in ReloadAsync and both unchanged.</para>
    ///
    /// <para><b>Why three and not six.</b> Six rows per section came to ~847px
    /// of workspace against ~610px of viewport, which put הגשות below the fold
    /// — so the page's second question could only be reached by scrolling past
    /// its first. An overview that hides a section to keep a longer preview has
    /// the trade backwards. Measured at this desktop height: three rows in each
    /// of the two stacked sections fits, four does not (~684px). The rest of
    /// each queue is one click away in the footer, which is what the footer is
    /// for.</para></summary>
    private const int PreviewCount = 3;

    /// <summary>The rail's collapsed depth. The same number, named separately
    /// because the rail's control expands in place rather than navigating.</summary>
    private const int PersonalCollapsedCount = PreviewCount;

    /// <summary>How many personal rows the collapsed rail is holding back,
    /// completed ones included — they are reachable only through the expander.</summary>
    private int HiddenPersonal =>
        Math.Max(0, _personalOpen.Count - PersonalCollapsedCount) + _personalDone.Count;

    /// <summary>The age at which the submissions screen unlocks "תזכורת
    /// למנחה" — and, not by coincidence, MentorAttention's own single
    /// threshold. Restated here only to classify a row; the gate itself lives
    /// on that screen and on the server, and this page performs no action.</summary>
    private const int ReminderThresholdDays = 3;

    // ── The section switcher ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Which single section is in focus, or null for all of them.
    ///
    /// <para>This replaced a four-way priority lens
    /// (הכל / דורש טיפול / באיחור / קרוב למועד) that was built for a Kanban
    /// board of four columns and did not outlive it. What a task workspace's
    /// switcher is for is focusing ONE queue, which is what the mentor's does
    /// and what this now does.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Priority did not leave with it: every tab carries its queue's
    /// size, and every row carries its waiting age on the shared ladder.</para></summary>
    private Section? _focus;

    private bool Shows(Section s) => _focus is null || _focus == s;

    /// <summary>True while either INCOMING queue is on screen, i.e. whenever
    /// the wide column has something to hold.</summary>
    private bool ShowsPrimary => Shows(Section.Requests) || Shows(Section.Approvals);

    /// <summary>The two-column row is the "הכל" composition. Every filter
    /// leaves exactly one column standing, and a two-track grid with one empty
    /// track is a half-width panel beside bare canvas — so the row goes
    /// single-track instead and the surviving panel takes the full width.</summary>
    private string WorkspaceClass => _focus is null ? "" : "lt-workspace-solo";

    /// <summary>The section's size, as MSectionHeading's count pill — the same
    /// `.motiva-count` bubble the filter tabs carry, so the two places this
    /// page prints a number are the same object. Empty at zero: a section
    /// already saying "אין בקשות שדורשות את החלטתך" does not also need a "0".</summary>
    private static string? CountLabel(int count) => count == 0 ? null : count.ToString();

    /// <summary>A panel in the wide column with nothing in it sizes to its own
    /// empty state instead of claiming an equal share of the column.</summary>
    private static string QuietWhenEmpty(int count) => count == 0 ? "lt-pane-quiet" : "";

    /// <summary>The switcher — the mentor's control and vocabulary, carrying
    /// this role's counts. A zero renders no badge at all, so a queue that has
    /// emptied stops advertising itself.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<MFilterTabs.Tab> FilterTabs => new[]
    {
        new MFilterTabs.Tab("",          "הכל"),
        new MFilterTabs.Tab("requests",  "בקשות",          _requests.Count),
        new MFilterTabs.Tab("approvals", "הגשות",          _approvals.Count),
        new MFilterTabs.Tab("personal",  "משימות אישיות",  _personalOpen.Count),
    };

    private string ActiveTabKey => _focus is null ? "" : Slug(_focus.Value);

    /// <summary>Selecting is not toggling: "הכל" is what clears.</summary>
    private void SelectFocus(string key)
    {
        _focus = FromSlug(key);
        _personalExpanded = false;
        RebuildVisiblePersonal();
    }

    private static string Slug(Section s) => s switch
    {
        Section.Requests  => "requests",
        Section.Approvals => "approvals",
        _                 => "personal",
    };

    private static Section? FromSlug(string? key) => key switch
    {
        "requests"  => Section.Requests,
        "approvals" => Section.Approvals,
        "personal"  => Section.Personal,
        _           => null,
    };

    // ── State ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private List<ProjectRequestRowDto>        _requests  = new();
    private List<PendingMentorApprovalRowDto> _approvals = new();

    private List<PersonalTaskDto> _personalOpen    = new();
    private List<PersonalTaskDto> _personalDone    = new();
    private List<PersonalTaskDto> _visiblePersonal = new();
    private bool _personalExpanded;

    /// <summary>Needed only to answer "is this person a mentor as well, and are
    /// they currently in מצב מנחה". Nothing on this page is gated on it — see
    /// GuidanceActive.</summary>
    [CascadingParameter] private User? _user { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The projects this user MENTORS, when guidance mode is on. Empty
    /// set and null mean different things: null is "not scoped", an empty set
    /// is "scoped, and nothing is in scope".</summary>
    private HashSet<int>? _guidanceProjectIds;

    private bool _loading = true;
    private int? _togglingId;

    private bool             _modalOpen;
    private PersonalTaskDto? _editing;

    /// <summary>The incoming item being inspected, or null for none. One field
    /// for both kinds, because there is one panel — see
    /// LecturerItemQuickView.Item for why the union is typed as object.</summary>
    private object? _inspecting;

    /// <summary>A click on an incoming row opens the panel. It does NOT
    /// navigate: the panel's own CTA does, to the same route the row used to go
    /// to directly.</summary>
    private void Inspect(object item) => _inspecting = item;

    private void CloseInspect() => _inspecting = null;

    private int OverdueCount => _personalOpen.Count(t => MentorTime.IsOverdue(t.DueDate));

    // ── Guidance scope ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether מצב מנחה ("guidance mode") is currently in effect FOR THIS USER.
    ///
    /// <para>This is a SCOPE switch and nothing more. The workspace itself is
    /// never gated on it: the page, its route, its panes and every one of its
    /// feeds exist in both modes, because a lecturer's queue does not stop
    /// being their queue when they put a mentor hat on.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Both halves of the test are load-bearing. UserModeService.CurrentMode
    /// is a process-wide static, so a Staff-only lecturer can be left holding a
    /// stale "mentor" value from a previous dual-role session; IsDualRole is what
    /// makes this false for anyone who has no guidance context to scope TO. That
    /// matters beyond tidiness — api/dashboard?scope=mentor answers a Staff-only
    /// caller with the LECTURER scope, so filtering on its answer for such a user
    /// would narrow nothing while looking like it had.</para></summary>
    private bool GuidanceActive =>
        UserModeService.IsDualRole(_user)
        && UserModeService.EffectiveMode(_user) == UserModes.Mentor;

    /// <summary>Scoping predicate for the two project-keyed feeds that guidance
    /// mode narrows. Passes everything when guidance is off, which is what makes
    /// the default view the full lecturer queue.</summary>
    private bool InGuidanceScope(int projectId) =>
        _guidanceProjectIds is null || _guidanceProjectIds.Contains(projectId);

    // ── Loading ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        await ReloadAsync();
        UserModeService.CurrentModeChanged += OnModeChanged;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Three independent GETs, issued together rather than in sequence: none of
    /// them needs another's answer, and awaiting them one at a time would make
    /// the page as slow as their sum.
    ///
    /// <para>Each service already swallows its own transport failure and
    /// answers null, so one feed being down empties its panel and leaves the
    /// others intact — the page never fails whole.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>It was four. The lecturer-scoped Overview call fed צוותים בסיכון
    /// and nothing else, so it left with that section; the mentor-scoped
    /// Overview call below is a different question and stays.</para></summary>
    private async Task ReloadAsync()
    {
        var requestsTask  = Requests.GetAllAsync();
        var approvalsTask = Approvals.GetPendingAsync();
        var personalTask  = PersonalTasks.GetAsync();

        // The guidance scope, and ONLY when there is one to fetch. This is the
        // one call that depends on mode; it narrows two feeds and gates nothing.
        // Same endpoint the mentor dashboard reads, with the scope resolved
        // server-side from the caller's own roles — no new API, and no way for
        // this page to widen what the user may see.
        var guidanceTask = GuidanceActive ? Overview.GetAsync("mentor") : null;

        await Task.WhenAll(requestsTask, approvalsTask, personalTask);

        // Null when guidance is off, so InGuidanceScope passes everything and
        // the default view is the complete lecturer queue.
        _guidanceProjectIds = guidanceTask is null
            ? null
            : (await guidanceTask)?.Projects.Select(p => p.ProjectId).ToHashSet();

        // The product's own classifier decides what is the lecturer's — see the
        // header note. Longest-waiting first: the panel scrolls, so nothing is
        // hidden, and the row that has waited longest on a decision is the one
        // that should meet the eye first. /management/requests still owns the
        // full set and its own order; no filter, scope or count moved.
        _requests = (await requestsTask ?? new())
            .Where(r => IsAwaitingLecturer(r.Status))
            .Where(r => InGuidanceScope(r.ProjectId))
            .OrderBy(r => r.CreatedAt)
            .ToList();

        // Longest wait first: the whole point of this inbox is the one that has
        // been stuck longest, and DaysWaiting is the server's own figure.
        _approvals = (await approvalsTask ?? new())
            .Where(a => InGuidanceScope(a.ProjectId))
            .OrderByDescending(a => a.DaysWaiting)
            .ToList();

        SplitPersonal(await personalTask);

        _loading = false;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// RequestsManagement.BucketOf()'s "decision" bucket, restated as a
    /// predicate.
    ///
    /// <para>Written as an exclusion of the two buckets that are NOT the
    /// lecturer's rather than a list of the five that are, so a status added to
    /// RequestStatuses later shows up here by default. A new status is far more
    /// likely to be another thing waiting on staff than another terminal or
    /// mentor state, and a request that wrongly appears is noticed; one that
    /// silently never appears is not.</para></summary>
    private static bool IsAwaitingLecturer(string status) =>
        status is not (RequestStatuses.Resolved
                    or RequestStatuses.Closed
                    or RequestStatuses.PendingMentorRecommendation);

    // ── Personal tasks ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private void SplitPersonal(IEnumerable<PersonalTaskDto> all)
    {
        var list = all.ToList();

        _personalOpen = list.Where(t => !t.IsDone)
                            .OrderBy(t => t.DueDate ?? DateTime.MaxValue)
                            .ToList();

        _personalDone = list.Where(t => t.IsDone)
                            .OrderByDescending(t => t.CreatedAt)
                            .ToList();

        RebuildVisiblePersonal();
    }

    /// <summary>Collapsed shows OPEN tasks only, capped at
    /// PersonalCollapsedCount. Expanded shows everything, completed last — so a
    /// row that was just ticked is still reachable rather than disappearing
    /// with its own undo.
    ///
    /// <para>The cap no longer varies with the filter. It used to fall to the
    /// page-wide preview cap under "הכל", which existed because four sections
    /// shared one scroll; the rail now scrolls on its own, so the collapsed
    /// depth is the same in every filter — MentorTasksPage's rule.</para></summary>
    private void RebuildVisiblePersonal() =>
        _visiblePersonal = _personalExpanded
            ? _personalOpen.Concat(_personalDone).ToList()
            : _personalOpen.Take(PersonalCollapsedCount).ToList();

    private void TogglePersonalExpanded()
    {
        _personalExpanded = !_personalExpanded;
        RebuildVisiblePersonal();
    }

    private async Task ToggleAsync(int id)
    {
        _togglingId = id;
        var ok = await PersonalTasks.ToggleAsync(id);
        _togglingId = null;

        if (!ok) return;

        // Flip locally rather than refetching every feed to learn one bit.
        var all = _personalOpen.Concat(_personalDone).ToList();
        var hit = all.FirstOrDefault(t => t.Id == id);
        if (hit is not null) hit.IsDone = !hit.IsDone;
        SplitPersonal(all);
    }

    private void OpenNewTask()
    {
        _editing   = null;
        _modalOpen = true;
    }

    private void OpenEditTask(PersonalTaskDto task)
    {
        _editing   = task;
        _modalOpen = true;
    }

    private void CloseModal()
    {
        _modalOpen = false;
        _editing   = null;
    }

    private void OnTaskSaved(PersonalTaskDto saved)
    {
        var all = _personalOpen.Concat(_personalDone).ToList();
        if (!all.Any(t => t.Id == saved.Id)) all.Add(saved);

        SplitPersonal(all);
        CloseModal();
    }

    private void OnTaskDeleted(int deletedId)
    {
        SplitPersonal(_personalOpen.Concat(_personalDone).Where(t => t.Id != deletedId));
        CloseModal();
    }

    // ── Row state chips ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// The row's one state chip, sitting at the reading start of the context
    /// line so the states align down a column and can be read without reading
    /// the titles.
    ///
    /// <para>Neutral by default, and that is the change: every row used to
    /// carry a tinted chip, which spent the page's colour budget on the fact
    /// that a row exists. Rose is now reserved for a genuine escalation — a
    /// submission past the shared reminder threshold, an at-risk team's health
    /// score, an overdue personal task — so red on this page always means the
    /// same thing.</para></summary>
    private static RenderFragment AgeChip(string label, MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant variant) => @<MStatusBadge
        Size="MStatusBadge.BadgeSize.Small"
        Variant="@variant"
        Text="@label" />;

    /// <summary>
    /// How long a request has been open, in browser-local calendar days.
    ///
    /// <para><b>Why this is computed here and not read from the DTO.</b>
    /// <c>ProjectRequestRowDto</c> carries no server-side waiting age —
    /// only submissions do, via <c>DaysWaiting</c>. The row's chip has always
    /// printed a browser-local age anyway (MentorTime.AgoLabel reads the same
    /// CreatedAt the same way), so this adds no clock that was not already on
    /// screen; it lets the chip's COLOUR agree with the text beside it instead
    /// of contradicting it.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>It is deliberately NOT added back to <c>MentorTime</c>, which had
    /// exactly this helper removed on purpose: the harm there was four call
    /// sites comparing a local age against two different hardcoded thresholds.
    /// This one is compared against <c>MentorAttention.AgeOf</c> — the single
    /// shared threshold — and nothing else. The durable fix is a server-computed
    /// WaitingDays on the request row, which is a server change this pass does
    /// not make.</para></summary>
    private static int DaysOpen(ProjectRequestRowDto r) =>
        Math.Max(0, (int)(DateTime.Now.Date - r.CreatedAt.ToLocalTime().Date).TotalDays);

    /// <summary>A personal task's deadline chip. Null when the task carries no
    /// due date, so a task without one simply has no chip — the same rule
    /// MentorTasksPage applies.</summary>
    private RenderFragment? DueChip(PersonalTaskDto t)
    {
        var label = MentorTime.DeadlineLabel(t.DueDate);
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(label)) return null;

        var variant =
            t.IsDone                            ? MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant.Neutral
            : MentorTime.IsOverdue(t.DueDate)   ? MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant.Rose
                                                : MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant.Neutral;

        return @<MStatusBadge Size="MStatusBadge.BadgeSize.Small" Variant="@variant" Text="@label" />;
    }

    // ── Row copy ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// The context line's ONE fact — the first of the two that is actually
    /// present.
    ///
    /// <para>This replaced a "team · project" chain, and the reason is the
    /// board: with the three feeds side by side, a project title long enough to
    /// need its own line ("Motiva — Final Project Management Platform") pushed
    /// every column into ellipsis and made three rows read as one paragraph.
    /// Team names are short and recognisable, which is why the team leads
    /// wherever there is one; the fact that loses is never lost, it moves to
    /// the row's hover and to the screen the row opens.</para></summary>
    private static string OneOf(string? first, string? second) =>
        !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(first)  ? first!.Trim()
        : !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(second) ? second!.Trim()
        : "";

    /// <summary>Everything the row deliberately does not print, joined for its
    /// hover. Blanks fall out, so a row with no mentor and no milestone simply
    /// has a shorter tooltip rather than a string of separators.</summary>
    private static string Details(params string?[] parts) =>
        string.Join(" · ", parts.Where(v => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(v))
                                .Select(v => v!.Trim()));

    /// <summary>
    /// A request's type, IN HEBREW OR NOT AT ALL.
    ///
    /// <para><c>RequestTypes.Label</c> falls back to returning the raw
    /// identifier for a type it does not know, which is right for a screen
    /// that must not silently drop a value — but live and seeded rows carry
    /// types outside the Shared constant list, so putting it straight on a row
    /// printed "ScopeChange" and "SpecialResource" in English in the middle of
    /// a Hebrew column.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>A context line is an aid, not a record: when there is no Hebrew
    /// word for the type, the row simply shows its team instead. The exact
    /// value is still on the row's hover and on the requests screen, so
    /// nothing is lost — and no list, filter or constant is touched.</para></summary>
    private static string? TypeLabel(string type) =>
        RequestTypes.All.Contains(type) ? RequestTypes.Label(type) : null;

    /// <summary>"מנחה: …" for the tooltip, or nothing when no mentor is
    /// assigned. Named rather than inlined so the two feeds that mention a
    /// mentor word it identically.</summary>
    private static string? MentorLabel(string? names) =>
        string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(names) ? null : $"מנחה: {names.Trim()}";

    /// <summary>
    /// How long something has been waiting — the wording BOTH incoming feeds
    /// now use, on the row and in the panel.
    ///
    /// <para>The requests chip used to print MentorTime.AgoLabel ("לפני 134
    /// ימים"), which answers a different question: when the request was
    /// opened, not how long it has been waiting on anyone. Beside a chip that
    /// escalates, "לפני" reads as an event receding into the past while the
    /// colour insists something is getting worse. "ממתינה" says the thing the
    /// escalation is actually about.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>A WAIT, NEVER "באיחור". There is no deadline on a request or on a
    /// mentor approval, so nothing measured here can be late — the same
    /// distinction MentorAttention documents and MentorAging enforces by
    /// leaving lateness vocabulary out of its vocabulary entirely.</para></summary>
    private static string WaitingLabel(int days) => days switch
    {
        0 => "ממתינה היום",
        1 => "ממתינה יום",
        2 => "ממתינה יומיים",
        _ => $"ממתינה {days} ימים",
    };

    /// <summary>Flipping מצב מנחה changes what the two scoped feeds contain, so
    /// the page refetches rather than just repainting the rows it already had.
    /// It does NOT change whether the workspace is available — every pane is
    /// rendered in both modes.</summary>
    private void OnModeChanged() => InvokeAsync(async () =>
    {
        _loading = true;
        StateHasChanged();
        await ReloadAsync();
        StateHasChanged();
    });

    public void Dispose() => UserModeService.CurrentModeChanged -= OnModeChanged;
}
